      "summaries": {
        "en": "rag-from-scratch is a comprehensive educational project that demonstrates how to build a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system from the ground up, addressing the challenge of creating AI applications that can access and reason over external knowledge. It teaches the core RAG pipeline through hands-on Jupyter notebooks, covering document ingestion, vector search, and LLM integration with clear, modular code. Developers can use this as a practical blueprint to implement custom RAG solutions, experiment with different embedding models and retrievers, and adapt the architecture for domain-specific applications like document Q&A or knowledge bases.",
        "zh": "rag-from-scratch是一个开源教学项目，通过Jupyter Notebook逐步展示如何从零构建RAG系统。它涵盖文档加载、向量化存储、语义检索及与大语言模型集成的全流程，以模块化代码解析检索与生成的协同机制。项目可作为实践模板，支持替换嵌入模型或调整检索策略，便于快速开发定制化知识问答或文档分析应用，是学习现代AI架构的实用资源。",
        "es": "rag-from-scratch is a comprehensive educational project that demonstrates how to build a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system from the ground up, addressing the challenge of creating AI applications that can access and reason over external knowledge. It teaches the core RAG pipeline through hands-on Jupyter notebooks, covering document ingestion, vector search, and LLM integration with clear, modular code. Developers can use this as a practical blueprint to implement custom RAG solutions, experiment with different embedding models and retrievers, and adapt the architecture for domain-specific applications like document Q&A or knowledge bases.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "rag-from-scratch gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "rag-from-scratch is a comprehensive educational project that demonstrates how to build a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system from the ground up, addressing the challenge of creating AI applications that can access and reason over external knowledge. It teaches the core RAG pipeline through hands-on Jupyter notebooks, covering document ingestion, vector search, and LLM integration with clear, modular code. Developers can use this as a practical blueprint to implement custom RAG solutions, experiment with different embedding models and retrievers, and adapt the architecture for domain-specific applications like document Q&A or knowledge bases.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/langchain-ai/rag-from-scratch for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
